            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "About 50 minutes",
            "text": "<p>Mostly farro, and that number moves: pearled is about 15 minutes, semi-pearled 25, whole closer to 40. Check which you have before you plan around it.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "g_serves": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "users",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "Serves 2",
            "text": "<p>Two 6 oz fillets, one each, over a shared platter of the farro. It scales up cleanly &mdash; the only limit is how many fillets fit in one skillet without steaming.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "g_prep": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "The salad keeps four days",
            "text": "<p>Make it through the dressing and refrigerate, holding back the pear, parsley and hazelnuts. Cook the fish fresh &mdash; cooked fish is a three-day ingredient.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "g_marinade": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "heart",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "Thirty seconds of pressure",
            "text": "<p>Hold the fillets flat with a spatula as they go in. It is the difference between crackling skin and skin that curled away from the pan and stayed pale.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
