      "settings": {
        "section_id": "crispy-skin",
        "liquid": "<style>\n  .sea-sheet {\n    --ink: #171717;\n    --muted: #5c5c5c;\n    --line: #e5e2dc;\n    --wash: #faf8f4;\n    --gold: #bb8f50;\n    color: var(--ink);\n    background: var(--wash);\n    border: 1px solid var(--line);\n    border-radius: 20px;\n    padding: 30px;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__eyebrow {\n    font-size: 11px;\n    letter-spacing: .14em;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    color: var(--gold);\n    font-weight: 600;\n    margin: 0 0 8px;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__heading {\n    font-size: clamp(23px, 2.8vw, 30px);\n    line-height: 1.15;\n    font-weight: 600;\n    margin: 0 0 10px;\n    max-width: 22ch;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__lede {\n    font-size: 15px;\n    line-height: 1.55;\n    color: var(--muted);\n    margin: 0 0 24px;\n    max-width: 68ch;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__cols {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));\n    gap: 14px;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__col {\n    background: #fff;\n    border: 1px solid var(--line);\n    border-radius: 14px;\n    padding: 18px;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__col--pick {\n    border-color: var(--gold);\n    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--gold);\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__num {\n    display: inline-flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    width: 26px;\n    height: 26px;\n    border-radius: 50%;\n    background: var(--ink);\n    color: #fff;\n    font-size: 12px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    margin: 0 0 10px;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__col h3 {\n    font-size: 15.5px;\n    font-weight: 600;\n    line-height: 1.3;\n    margin: 0 0 7px;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__col p {\n    font-size: 13.5px;\n    line-height: 1.55;\n    color: var(--muted);\n    margin: 0;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__foot {\n    margin: 18px 0 0;\n    padding-top: 14px;\n    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);\n    font-size: 13px;\n    line-height: 1.55;\n    color: var(--muted);\n  }\n  @media (max-width: 749px) {\n    .sea-sheet {\n      padding: 22px;\n    }\n    .sea-sheet__cols {\n      grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n    }\n  }\n\n  .sea-sheet__fig {\n    margin: 22px 0 0;\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__fig img {\n    width: 100%;\n    height: auto;\n    display: block;\n    border-radius: 16px;\n    box-shadow: 0 14px 34px -22px rgba(0,0,0,.5);\n  }\n  .sea-sheet__figcap {\n    margin: 10px 0 0;\n    font-size: 12.5px;\n    line-height: 1.5;\n    color: var(--muted);\n  }\n</style>\n<div class=\"sea-sheet\">\n  <p class=\"sea-sheet__eyebrow\">The part that goes wrong</p>\n  <h2 class=\"sea-sheet__heading\">Branzino skin curls off the pan unless you hold it down.</h2>\n  <p class=\"sea-sheet__lede\">\n    Branzino fillets are thin and the skin contracts faster than the flesh, so the moment they hit\n    heat the edges lift and the middle never touches metal. You get a pale stripe down the centre\n    and no crackle. Thirty seconds of gentle pressure fixes it, and it is the only fiddly thing in\n    this recipe. We have a <a href=\"/blogs/seafood-recipes/seafood-101-the-secret-to-crispy-skin\">whole\n    Seafood 101 on crispy skin</a> if you want the long version.\n  </p>\n\n  <div class=\"sea-sheet__cols\">\n    <div class=\"sea-sheet__col sea-sheet__col--pick\">\n      <span class=\"sea-sheet__num\">1</span>\n      <h3>Dry, then oil &mdash; not butter</h3>\n      <p>Pat the fillets drier than feels necessary; skin will not crisp on a damp surface. Sear in\n      olive oil, because butter on its own at medium-high scorches its milk solids long before the\n      skin has set.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"sea-sheet__col\">\n      <span class=\"sea-sheet__num\">2</span>\n      <h3>Press for thirty seconds</h3>\n      <p>Lay the fillets in skin-side down and press gently with a fish spatula for the first half\n      minute, until they stop trying to curl. Then leave them completely alone for three to four\n      minutes.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"sea-sheet__col\">\n      <span class=\"sea-sheet__num\">3</span>\n      <h3>Butter at the flip, rest skin-up</h3>\n      <p>Flip, add the butter and baste for about a minute until just opaque. Rest skin-side up\n      &mdash; put a crisp fillet down on a plate and the trapped steam undoes everything you just\n      did.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <figure class=\"sea-sheet__fig\">\n    <img\n      src=\"{{ '20260825-Stetten-Wilson-196.jpg' | file_url }}\"\n      alt=\"A fish spatula pressing branzino fillets skin-side down in a cast-iron skillet\"\n      width=\"1200\"\n      height=\"1600\"\n      loading=\"lazy\"\n      decoding=\"async\">\n    <figcaption class=\"sea-sheet__figcap\">\n      Gentle, even pressure across the fillet &mdash; you are flattening it against the pan, not\n      squashing it. It releases on its own when the skin is ready.\n    </figcaption>\n  </figure>\n</div>\n",
        "padding_top": 24,
        "padding_bottom": 24,
        "divider": false,
        "narrow": false,
        "rounded": false,
