    "meal_prep": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "m_sub": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Make it ahead",
            "subheading_size": "subtitle-md",
            "secondary_color": true
          }
        },
        "m_head": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Dress it off the heat",
            "heading_size": "title-md",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "m_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Once the farro has gone into the skillet with the mushrooms and onion, take the pan off the burner before the miso dressing goes anywhere near it. Miso is a live, fermented paste and its flavour flattens in a hot pan &mdash; you lose the savoury edge that makes the salad worth eating cold the next day.</p><p>The same logic applies to the order of everything else. Hazelnuts get toasted first so they are out of the way, the pear is sliced and held in lemon, and the fish is the very last thing to touch heat.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "m_btn": {
          "type": "button",
          "settings": {
            "button_label": "Shop Branzino",
            "button_link": "/products/branzino-bundle-2x-6oz-portions",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_size": "md",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "m_sub",
        "m_head",
        "m_text",
        "m_btn"
      ],
